[{"id":78806,"sender_id":396,"sender_full_name":"jim stasheff","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/eeb50cc40b4c9eb22828309e0a393351?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Contraction.20as.20.28co.29derivation/near/78806\">#1</a> The n-lab is very clear on contraction as a derivation<br>For example, there is a contraction of a vector $X\\in V$ and a $n$-form $\\omega\\in \\Lambda V^*$:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(X,\\omega)\\mapsto \\iota_X(\\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">↦</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ι</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>and $\\iota_X: \\omega\\mapsto \\iota_X(\\omega)$ is a graded derivation of the exterior algebra of degree $-1$. This is also done for the tangent bundle which is a $C^\\infty(M)$-module $V = T M$, then one gets the contraction of vector fields and differential forms. It can also be done in vector spaces, fibrewise.  </p>\n<p>Is it written  somewhere about contraction of a $1$-form $\\omega$ with an$n-vector $X\\in \\in \\Lambda V$ as a coderivation?</p>","timestamp":1567779298,"subject":"Contraction as (co)derivation","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]